n live on the  streets on checks from the government  but at the same time this is also kind  of negative as well  if you're able to carry on daily life by  doing nothing a good amount of people  will choose to do nothing for example  take a listen to what this homeless man  thinks i mean if we're gonna be  realistic they pay you to be homeless  here when you said that san francisco  pays people to be homeless what did you  mean by that  you mean that literally yeah  i mean i get 620 bucks a month dude  from general assistance or would you how  was that hard to get  phone call bro  [ __ ] phone call 200 food stamps and  620 bucks cash a month wow forget about  it why wouldn't i do it and he's not the  only one who thinks like this  california's homeless programs are so  generous that homeless people from other  states immigrate to california to be  homeless there instead somehow  california has transitioned from being  the dream destination for entrepreneurs  to being the deepest nation for the  homeless not only does this drain the  resources of california but it also  makes everyday life for californians way  harder due to the large number of  homeless people it's common to find  human feces and drug needles across  their cities in fact this issue has  become so prevalent that san francisco  pays people 184 thousand dollars per  year to clean their sidewalks when you  have to do this you clearly have a  problem and i don't know about you but i  wouldn't want to go to work or have my  kids go to school in such an area  leaving the state is often the top  priority for anyone with any sort of  financial stability and as these middle  class upper middle class and high income  families leave the state the state is  simply driven further into the depths of  poverty  [Music]  given the circumstances in california i  don't think you'd be surprised here that  the population is on the decline but  it's not as drastic as you might think  and this brings up the question why d